1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:12,067
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:38,533 --> 00:00:40,567
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:42,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:44,733 --> 00:00:46,100
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,133 --> 00:00:56,467
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,433 --> 00:00:58,967
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,267
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:01,767
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:03,733
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:06,933
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:11,333
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:12,533 --> 00:01:16,667
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:18,733
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:21,733
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:22,433 --> 00:01:24,467
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:27,900
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:29,533 --> 00:01:31,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,367
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:34,767 --> 00:01:35,867
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,367 --> 00:01:38,600
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:38,733 --> 00:01:40,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:45,933 --> 00:01:48,533
<i> General Ricardo Jacinto!</i>

24
00:01:48,667 --> 00:01:52,067
<i>Are you done with the people
from Ginintuang Lupa?</i>

25
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:54,333
<i>Just because he stands
with the poor</i>

26
00:01:54,467 --> 00:01:56,633
<i>doesn't mean he can paint
my father as the villain.</i>

27
00:01:56,767 --> 00:01:59,833
<i>The Manila Telebalita reporter
is tearing my business apart.</i>

28
00:01:59,967 --> 00:02:01,067
<i> You know what to do.</i>

29
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:03,800
<i>I won't mess this up,
General Jacinto.</i>

30
00:02:03,933 --> 00:02:05,000
<i> Just scare him.</i>

31
00:02:05,133 --> 00:02:08,167
<i>He thinks we shot the man
during the demolition.</i>

32
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:09,567
<i> The goal is to keep</i>

33
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:14,167
<i> that bastard's mouth shut.</i>

34
00:02:14,333 --> 00:02:15,367
<i> I got the bike.</i>

35
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:18,033
<i>Rudy can finally
undergo surgery.</i>

36
00:02:18,167 --> 00:02:22,200
- [EKG BEEPING RAPIDLY]
- [RUDY GRUNTING]

37
00:02:22,333 --> 00:02:24,267
<i> Pa! Doc, help!</i>

38
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:26,200
<i>Doc, please do everything
to save my father!</i>

39
00:02:26,633 --> 00:02:27,500
<i> Pa!</i>

40
00:02:27,633 --> 00:02:30,100
<i>- Rudy!
- Pa! Pa!</i>

41
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,367
- [AGENT] Hey.
- [RALLOS] What's up?

42
00:02:40,033 --> 00:02:42,100
Hello. Tina, this is
for pick-up.

43
00:02:42,233 --> 00:02:43,333
Courier's on the way.

44
00:02:44,733 --> 00:02:45,800
Okay, sir.

45
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,333
Please log it here, sir.

46
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:52,767
- Thank you.
- Faster.

47
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:54,200
He's looking at us.

48
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:58,133
- Here's your ID, sir.
- Thank you.

49
00:02:58,267 --> 00:02:59,467
Come on, let's go.

50
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,800
Hold it right there.

51
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:08,667
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

52
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:09,800
Yes, sir?

53
00:03:17,267 --> 00:03:18,367
[BANGING LIGHTLY]

54
00:03:19,233 --> 00:03:20,367
You forgot this.

55
00:03:21,433 --> 00:03:23,633
- Oh!
- [BOTH GIGGLING]

56
00:03:23,767 --> 00:03:26,667
Thank you, sir. He's so clumsy.
[GIGGLING]

57
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,167
- Let's go, you.
- [LAUGHS]

58
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:30,500
[LAUGHING] Silly me!

59
00:03:30,633 --> 00:03:33,367
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

60
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:35,767
- [LAUGHS]
- Why did you leave it?

61
00:03:40,067 --> 00:03:42,300
[REYES] Ma'am Sam. Here's
the paper for the bike.

62
00:03:42,433 --> 00:03:46,633
[PAPER RUSTLING, THUDS]

63
00:03:46,767 --> 00:03:47,800
It's stolen?

64
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:51,267
We called the owner
that it's registered under.

65
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:53,000
Said it was stolen last year.

66
00:03:53,133 --> 00:03:57,533
And ma'am, his statements
match our records.

67
00:03:57,700 --> 00:04:00,333
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

68
00:04:00,467 --> 00:04:02,700
Alright. We can still do
other things.

69
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:06,033
We'll find out who is behind
this group soon.

70
00:04:06,167 --> 00:04:07,267
What a bummer.

71
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:09,433
That bike really drove me
to a corner.

72
00:04:10,133 --> 00:04:11,233
Bike?

73
00:04:11,733 --> 00:04:13,467
What kind of bike
are you talking about?

74
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:16,667
The bike of the man we met
at the bar.

75
00:04:17,233 --> 00:04:19,400
We'd like to find out
who he is.

76
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:21,167
Sam.

77
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:24,133
I told you I'll take care
of that man.

78
00:04:24,267 --> 00:04:25,333
Let me handle it.

79
00:04:25,467 --> 00:04:28,133
That guy's my problem.
I don't need your help.

80
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:31,400
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

81
00:04:31,533 --> 00:04:34,233
Uh-oh, a lovers' quarrel again?

82
00:04:37,633 --> 00:04:38,933
Wait a second.

83
00:04:39,067 --> 00:04:42,333
Do you have to be involved
with every thing I do?

84
00:04:43,067 --> 00:04:45,500
Sam, why is your tone like that?

85
00:04:45,633 --> 00:04:48,567
Is it because I got praised
and you got criticized?

86
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:49,667
Is that it?

87
00:04:50,133 --> 00:04:51,067
What?

88
00:04:51,733 --> 00:04:53,000
[SCOFFS] Excuse me?

89
00:04:53,133 --> 00:04:55,133
Why would I be mad
when our co-teammates

90
00:04:55,267 --> 00:04:56,633
get praised?

91
00:04:56,767 --> 00:04:58,967
Shouldn't I be happy?

92
00:04:59,233 --> 00:05:01,100
Can you please
just give me space.

93
00:05:01,267 --> 00:05:03,067
Space? Are you
in a relationship?

94
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:05,000
[SEBASTIAN EXHALES HEAVILY]

95
00:05:05,133 --> 00:05:06,200
Sam,

96
00:05:06,733 --> 00:05:09,500
don't you see the effort
I'm putting in?

97
00:05:09,633 --> 00:05:10,633
Huh?

98
00:05:11,367 --> 00:05:14,500
Because if you do,
you won't treat me this way.

99
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:16,500
Did I ask for you to do this?

100
00:05:18,033 --> 00:05:19,267
I didn't, did I?

101
00:05:19,667 --> 00:05:22,133
You know, no matter what you do,

102
00:05:22,567 --> 00:05:24,967
just don't. I can handle it
myself.

103
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:26,800
Alone.

104
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:33,767
- [KAREN] Space, space, space.
- [CHAIR CLATTERS]

105
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:37,067
There you go. Space, indeed.

106
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:44,167
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

107
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,067
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

108
00:05:56,867 --> 00:05:58,400
- Yes?
- [DOOR OPENS]

109
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:00,600
Sir.

110
00:06:01,233 --> 00:06:02,667
Can I talk to you?

111
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:03,833
Of course.

112
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:05,067
Take a seat.

113
00:06:09,533 --> 00:06:10,633
[CHAIR CLATTERS]

114
00:06:10,767 --> 00:06:12,033
[LAUGHS AWKWARDLY]

115
00:06:13,133 --> 00:06:15,133
Sir, to tell you the truth,
I feel really bad

116
00:06:15,267 --> 00:06:17,367
for disappointing you.

117
00:06:18,933 --> 00:06:21,333
I really want to make it up
to you but...

118
00:06:21,467 --> 00:06:23,533
I just don't know how.

119
00:06:23,667 --> 00:06:25,467
[LAUGHING] Sam,

120
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:28,200
don't be too harsh on yourself.

121
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:31,000
Everybody makes mistakes.

122
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:33,300
We all trip, we all fall.

123
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:35,367
It's part of the job.

124
00:06:35,833 --> 00:06:38,900
[SAM] About the gold
smuggling case.

125
00:06:39,333 --> 00:06:42,100
I really want us to close
that case

126
00:06:42,267 --> 00:06:44,533
and to hold those
who are involved accountable.

127
00:06:44,667 --> 00:06:46,500
Yes, I know. You are capable.

128
00:06:47,733 --> 00:06:50,500
Sir, I just thought, what if we
form a small team?

129
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,467
Let's start with that.

130
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:54,300
So that from there,
we could know--

131
00:06:54,433 --> 00:06:55,467
[PIA CLEARS THROAT]

132
00:06:56,733 --> 00:06:57,667
Sorry.

133
00:06:58,033 --> 00:06:59,400
The door was left open.

134
00:06:59,533 --> 00:07:02,333
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

135
00:07:02,467 --> 00:07:03,767
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

136
00:07:04,433 --> 00:07:06,400
I overheard your conversation
as well.

137
00:07:07,167 --> 00:07:09,167
I'm utterly impressed, Jacinto.

138
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,467
Pia.

139
00:07:12,167 --> 00:07:13,133
Sir.

140
00:07:13,567 --> 00:07:14,533
[DELGADO] Hmm?

141
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:17,433
Are we trying to pull as many
strings as we can

142
00:07:17,567 --> 00:07:19,333
here in the NCIA?

143
00:07:19,467 --> 00:07:21,133
I'm just merely volunteering
to do something

144
00:07:21,267 --> 00:07:23,400
that I know I'm capable
of solving.

145
00:07:23,533 --> 00:07:26,267
Pia, Sam is perfectly capable.

146
00:07:26,667 --> 00:07:28,567
Sir, with all due respect,

147
00:07:28,833 --> 00:07:31,567
this one right here needs
to undergo retraining.

148
00:07:31,700 --> 00:07:33,167
Has she already done that?

149
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:34,900
As far as I know, she hasn't.

150
00:07:35,033 --> 00:07:36,133
Sir, I just realized.

151
00:07:36,267 --> 00:07:38,267
If I were to complete
the retraining,

152
00:07:38,933 --> 00:07:40,867
those groups might have already
come up with a plan against us!

153
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,667
The NCIA will still do its job.

154
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:45,000
Just not depending on you
this time.

155
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:47,200
Isn't that right,
Director Delgado?

156
00:07:47,333 --> 00:07:51,100
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

157
00:07:51,267 --> 00:07:52,400
[INHALES SHARPLY]

158
00:07:53,167 --> 00:07:54,500
You know, Sam,

159
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,767
Pia is right.

160
00:07:59,133 --> 00:08:01,900
I order you not to dig into
the case any further.

161
00:08:02,933 --> 00:08:05,133
I'll let a different agent
take care of it.

162
00:08:05,267 --> 00:08:06,800
But sir, what about
the suspects?

163
00:08:06,933 --> 00:08:09,667
[PIA] And we're still waiting...

164
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:12,600
for the committee's decision
on your suspension.

165
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:14,300
Right?

166
00:08:14,933 --> 00:08:16,933
We'll surely catch them

167
00:08:17,067 --> 00:08:18,633
but as of now,

168
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:23,367
while the committee is still
deciding on your case,

169
00:08:23,533 --> 00:08:25,867
you're not allowed
to be involved.

170
00:08:27,067 --> 00:08:28,567
Do you understand?

171
00:08:28,700 --> 00:08:35,667
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

172
00:08:36,567 --> 00:08:39,100
[EKG MONITOR BEEPING]

173
00:08:41,067 --> 00:08:48,033
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

174
00:08:49,167 --> 00:08:50,933
Doc, how's my father?

175
00:08:51,067 --> 00:08:52,133
Is he safe now?

176
00:08:52,733 --> 00:08:53,667
[DOCTOR] I'll be honest
with you.

177
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:55,800
Until the patient hasn't gone
under surgery,

178
00:08:55,967 --> 00:08:58,167
- [SOBBING]
- his condition will worsen.

179
00:08:58,300 --> 00:08:59,667
The next time this happens,

180
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:02,033
we might not be able
to save him any more.

181
00:09:02,367 --> 00:09:04,033
It is time we're up against.

182
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:05,467
Excuse me.

183
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:10,033
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

184
00:09:10,167 --> 00:09:13,100
[SIGHS] Did you hear
what the doctor said, Gabo?

185
00:09:14,133 --> 00:09:17,567
Time is running out
for your father.

186
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:19,867
To be able to save him,

187
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:22,267
to be able to have him
undergo an operation,

188
00:09:23,867 --> 00:09:26,100
we need money.

189
00:09:26,233 --> 00:09:28,367
[SOBBING CONTINUES]

190
00:09:28,533 --> 00:09:29,433
Why? [CRYING]

191
00:09:29,567 --> 00:09:32,333
Isn't Gabo doing
everything he can

192
00:09:32,467 --> 00:09:35,100
to able to fund
his father's operation?

193
00:09:35,233 --> 00:09:37,367
Why do you have to put
everything on his shoulder--

194
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:40,133
Who else are we depending on?!

195
00:09:40,533 --> 00:09:42,900
No one's helping us anyway!

196
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:45,400
[BETCHAY SNIFFLES]

197
00:09:46,333 --> 00:09:47,967
[VOICE BREAKING, SOBBING]
Well...

198
00:09:49,167 --> 00:09:53,000
It's not like your father
expects anything of you either.

199
00:09:57,467 --> 00:09:59,567
[BETCHAY SOBS]

200
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:03,200
[BETCHAY SOBS]

201
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,233
Don't worry.

202
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:12,500
I'm not coming back here
without any money.

203
00:10:18,667 --> 00:10:19,600
Gabo!

204
00:10:19,733 --> 00:10:26,633
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

205
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:38,600
What's the news?

206
00:10:38,733 --> 00:10:40,367
Lawin? Uwak?

207
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:42,267
We came back from NCIA.

208
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:45,633
We observed
and eavesdropped, Pops.

209
00:10:45,767 --> 00:10:47,000
Positive, Pops.

210
00:10:47,133 --> 00:10:48,133
A man caused a disturbance

211
00:10:48,267 --> 00:10:49,700
when they were about
to arrest Tiger.

212
00:10:49,833 --> 00:10:52,533
The man caught him first,
but he escaped

213
00:10:52,667 --> 00:10:54,067
as soon as the NCIA arrived.

214
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:56,133
- It might be Gabo.
- Hmm.

215
00:10:56,267 --> 00:10:58,533
He was about to catch Tiger.

216
00:10:58,667 --> 00:11:00,667
The NCIA is also
looking for him.

217
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:04,767
They're checking on why
he's chasing Tiger.

218
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:07,100
Gabo's life has been
put in jeopardy.

219
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:09,133
Even the NCIA

220
00:11:10,067 --> 00:11:11,400
wants to find him.

221
00:11:11,533 --> 00:11:12,333
Pops.

222
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:15,667
Why don't you give Gabo
another chance?

223
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:22,800
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

224
00:11:24,833 --> 00:11:27,933
- [CHEERING, LAUGHTER]
- [TEKLA] It's successful!

225
00:11:28,067 --> 00:11:29,933
[DABOY] Guys, have some snack!

226
00:11:30,067 --> 00:11:32,167
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

227
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:33,867
[TEKLA] Open it.

228
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,300
Why don't you do it?

229
00:11:35,433 --> 00:11:36,367
Hey!

230
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:39,867
[WHOOPING]

231
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:40,900
Where's Gabo?

232
00:11:41,067 --> 00:11:43,600
- Elton, grab a drink with us!
- [CHEERING]

233
00:11:43,733 --> 00:11:44,533
- C'mon!
- Yeah!

234
00:11:44,667 --> 00:11:46,600
Stop joking around.
You know what,

235
00:11:46,733 --> 00:11:49,833
if I find out that you're
covering for Gabo,

236
00:11:49,967 --> 00:11:51,567
I'll include you
in my police report.

237
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:54,000
- Hey!
- C'mon, Elton!

238
00:11:54,133 --> 00:11:56,233
Relax, relax!

239
00:11:56,367 --> 00:11:58,033
How could I?

240
00:11:58,433 --> 00:12:00,100
Gabo owes me a huge debt!

241
00:12:00,233 --> 00:12:02,100
Gabo won't let you down!

242
00:12:02,233 --> 00:12:05,500
He did everything he could
to get that motorcycle back.

243
00:12:05,633 --> 00:12:07,033
- Yes!
- He's right!

244
00:12:07,167 --> 00:12:08,267
He has the motorcycle?

245
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:12,000
- Yes!
- Absolutely!

246
00:12:12,133 --> 00:12:14,200
Relax, Elton!

247
00:12:14,333 --> 00:12:15,967
He'll give it back.

248
00:12:16,133 --> 00:12:18,500
You just have to trust him.

249
00:12:18,633 --> 00:12:20,367
How could I trust him?

250
00:12:20,967 --> 00:12:22,733
He seems so sketchy!

251
00:12:22,867 --> 00:12:25,633
What's he doing?
Why did he use the motorcycle?

252
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:27,867
- It's a secret!
- A secret...

253
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,467
- ...tary! Secretary!
- A secretary!

254
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:33,233
- Yeah!
- His handwriting is beautiful.

255
00:12:33,367 --> 00:12:35,333
Stop messing with me.

256
00:12:35,467 --> 00:12:38,267
Just make sure
the motorcycle is with him!

257
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,300
Because if not,

258
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:41,900
I'll file a report against you.

259
00:12:42,033 --> 00:12:44,767
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

260
00:12:47,767 --> 00:12:50,833
[BETCHAY] This is
for patient Rudy Magtibay.

261
00:12:50,967 --> 00:12:53,733
The one staying in the ICU.
This is for his surgery.

262
00:12:54,233 --> 00:12:57,400
Here's the partial payment.

263
00:13:00,433 --> 00:13:01,533
I'm sorry,

264
00:13:01,667 --> 00:13:06,333
but this isn't enough for
the patient's initial payment.

265
00:13:06,467 --> 00:13:09,367
Uh... ma'am...

266
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:11,900
Maybe you could allow
the surgery to happen?

267
00:13:12,033 --> 00:13:15,467
I promise we'll pay!

268
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:16,967
Just please let
the surgery happen.

269
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:21,600
I'm sorry, ma'am, but
the hospital won't allow that.

270
00:13:21,767 --> 00:13:28,700
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

271
00:13:36,867 --> 00:13:37,800
[MAMENG] Oh.

272
00:13:38,633 --> 00:13:40,600
Why the long face?

273
00:13:41,067 --> 00:13:42,533
I went to the cashier.

274
00:13:43,067 --> 00:13:45,500
I was about to pay
for Rudy's surgery.

275
00:13:46,267 --> 00:13:47,400
But it's not enough.

276
00:13:47,533 --> 00:13:50,100
Wait a minute, his surgery?

277
00:13:50,233 --> 00:13:52,100
Where did you get the money?

278
00:13:52,233 --> 00:13:54,533
Do you remember the girl
who came over?

279
00:13:54,900 --> 00:13:58,333
- Yes.
- She said she wanted to help.

280
00:13:59,333 --> 00:14:00,733
I asked for help.

281
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:02,633
She gave me money,
and I accepted it.

282
00:14:02,767 --> 00:14:03,767
What?!

283
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:05,167
You talked to that woman?

284
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:10,567
She said she wanted to settle.

285
00:14:10,700 --> 00:14:11,833
So I did.

286
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:13,600
Oh no.

287
00:14:13,733 --> 00:14:16,700
You went to settle the agreement
all by yourself?

288
00:14:16,833 --> 00:14:17,800
Gosh.

289
00:14:17,933 --> 00:14:23,233
It's like you sold
your honor and your dignity.

290
00:14:25,133 --> 00:14:26,333
What was I suppose to do?!

291
00:14:26,467 --> 00:14:30,133
What's the point of any of that?
Rudy is dying!

292
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:32,900
We're talking about
someone's life here!

293
00:14:33,033 --> 00:14:35,667
Honor and dignity are
completely worthless now.

294
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:38,400
Gabo is already working on
getting the money!

295
00:14:38,533 --> 00:14:41,533
I believe he can do it!

296
00:14:42,133 --> 00:14:43,667
That's enough.

297
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:46,767
I know he won't let Rudy die!

298
00:14:47,067 --> 00:14:48,967
That's enough!

299
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:52,400
I already gave up on Gabo!

300
00:14:54,433 --> 00:14:56,300
I hope I turn out wrong.

301
00:14:57,800 --> 00:15:00,667
That's what I'm praying for.

302
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,533
I wish he could find a way

303
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:06,767
to save his father's life.

304
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:11,667
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

305
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:18,800
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
- [MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVS]

306
00:15:29,133 --> 00:15:34,500
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVS]

307
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:40,700
[ENGINE HUMMING,
TURNS OFF]

308
00:15:42,367 --> 00:15:44,967
Gabo, what are you doing here?

309
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:48,900
Didn't we agree you
shouldn't come unless called?

310
00:15:52,267 --> 00:15:53,400
Where's Tatang?

311
00:15:53,533 --> 00:15:57,367
You've got some nerve showing
up here after screwing up.

312
00:15:57,500 --> 00:16:00,000
I need Tatang, not you guys.

313
00:16:00,133 --> 00:16:05,900
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

314
00:16:06,033 --> 00:16:07,133
Tatang!

315
00:16:08,333 --> 00:16:09,400
Tatang!

316
00:16:10,400 --> 00:16:11,400
Tatang!

317
00:16:11,533 --> 00:16:13,367
Gabo, so you're here.

318
00:16:14,633 --> 00:16:15,833
Where's Tatang?

319
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:23,200
What do you need, Gabo?

320
00:16:23,333 --> 00:16:27,100
Mister Tomas, Mister Omeng,
I really need your help.

321
00:16:27,233 --> 00:16:30,467
My father's in the hospital.
I need money.

322
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:33,900
You failed your first mission,
Gabo.

323
00:16:34,033 --> 00:16:36,100
I know that.

324
00:16:36,233 --> 00:16:38,267
But please give me
another chance.

325
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,700
Maybe you have another
mission for me.

326
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:43,233
There are plenty of missions
for you.

327
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:45,967
Like Pops said,
he chose you.

328
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:49,267
You know, Gabo,
you're very lucky.

329
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:52,833
Only a few passed
Pops's tests.

330
00:16:52,967 --> 00:16:55,033
Don't let him down.

331
00:16:58,533 --> 00:17:00,767
Come on, follow me.

332
00:17:05,467 --> 00:17:09,900
[KAREN] We need a sketch
of what the guy looks like...

333
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:14,933
- [CLEARS THROAT]
- Ma'am Sam.

334
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:18,233
Why were you in
Sir Delgado's office?

335
00:17:20,233 --> 00:17:22,667
I wanted to revisit
the gold smuggling case,

336
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:25,900
but Sir Delgado said no.

337
00:17:26,033 --> 00:17:28,300
He told me to stay hands-off.

338
00:17:28,433 --> 00:17:31,333
If Ma'am Pia's report
wasn't so sloppy,

339
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:33,800
we wouldn't be having
this problem.

340
00:17:34,933 --> 00:17:39,267
Because this screw-up of mine
is embarrassing for my dad.

341
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:42,667
Imagine General Jacinto...

342
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:44,967
having an inefficient agent
for a daughter.

343
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:46,867
It's tough being in
your position.

344
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:50,533
Your hands are tied. You have
no choice but to give up.

345
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:57,167
[MUSIC BECOMES REFLECTIVE]

346
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:08,567
No. I won't give up
on this case.

347
00:18:10,933 --> 00:18:15,000
Ma'am Sam, disobeying
Sir Delgado is dangerous.

348
00:18:15,133 --> 00:18:17,367
If that's what it takes,
I'll do it.

349
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:21,933
To prove to NCIA that
I'm a good agent, I'll do it.

350
00:18:23,033 --> 00:18:25,767
But I can't pull this off alone.

351
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:27,600
I still need your help.

352
00:18:29,467 --> 00:18:32,833
Ma'am, your team is here
for you.

353
00:18:32,967 --> 00:18:34,700
One for all.
All for one.

354
00:18:34,833 --> 00:18:37,300
Yeah, because you can't
do this by yourself.

355
00:18:40,333 --> 00:18:42,467
Thanks, guys.

356
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:45,933
But let's keep this from
Sir Delgado for now...

357
00:18:46,067 --> 00:18:48,500
until we finish this case.

358
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:51,467
You know me.

359
00:18:51,600 --> 00:18:54,333
I don't like having mistakes
on my record.

360
00:18:54,500 --> 00:18:57,667
You know how I am.
Keep the line straight

361
00:18:57,800 --> 00:19:00,600
and the plan detailed.

362
00:19:00,733 --> 00:19:05,733
If a mistake was made...
it needs to be fixed.

363
00:19:05,867 --> 00:19:12,767
[RESOLUTE MUSIC SWELLS]

364
00:19:14,533 --> 00:19:15,333
[DOOR CLICKS]

365
00:19:18,267 --> 00:19:19,733
You wanted to see me?

366
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,300
Have a seat.

367
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:29,633
Is there a problem?

368
00:19:30,167 --> 00:19:34,767
I want to talk to you about Sam.

369
00:19:35,733 --> 00:19:37,433
She's...

370
00:19:38,967 --> 00:19:40,400
going through a lot right now.

371
00:19:40,533 --> 00:19:42,467
She needs
her own support system.

372
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:45,333
I don't want
to see her so down.

373
00:19:45,467 --> 00:19:46,933
And...

374
00:19:47,067 --> 00:19:51,000
I don't want NCIA
to lose a great agent.

375
00:19:51,133 --> 00:19:52,300
Yes.

376
00:19:52,433 --> 00:19:56,067
I understand that you treat her
like your own daughter.

377
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:59,267
- I'm actually her best friend.
- [DELGADO] Hmm.

378
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:01,933
Hopefully, our operations
can go back to normal.

379
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:05,200
Don't mention this to her.

380
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:06,933
This might fall through.

381
00:20:07,333 --> 00:20:09,367
I don't want
to give her false hope.

382
00:20:10,533 --> 00:20:13,133
I have spoken
to the committee...

383
00:20:14,667 --> 00:20:16,533
about canceling her suspension.

384
00:20:17,133 --> 00:20:18,267
Really?

385
00:20:18,767 --> 00:20:19,900
Thank you.

386
00:20:20,033 --> 00:20:24,933
That's why, if you think

387
00:20:25,067 --> 00:20:27,867
she has a problem
that I can help with,

388
00:20:28,567 --> 00:20:30,200
let me know right away.

389
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:31,500
Yes, sir.

390
00:20:31,833 --> 00:20:33,000
I'll do that.

391
00:20:38,767 --> 00:20:39,933
You may leave.

392
00:20:40,067 --> 00:20:41,700
Oh! [CHUCKLES]

393
00:20:42,367 --> 00:20:43,700
Thank you, sir.

394
00:20:44,967 --> 00:20:49,633
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

395
00:20:49,767 --> 00:20:52,000
Ma'am Sam, what's the plan?

396
00:20:54,433 --> 00:20:55,567
[KAREN CLEARS THROAT]

397
00:20:57,133 --> 00:21:00,167
The one transacting
with Victor Zafra, Mr. Chan,

398
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:03,500
he will be our key to holding
Alias Tiger accountable.

399
00:21:04,467 --> 00:21:06,967
Borromeo has already
gone there to scout.

400
00:21:07,100 --> 00:21:08,333
You're right.

401
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:09,867
Once he speaks up,

402
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:11,800
the case against Zafra
will become much stronger.

403
00:21:11,933 --> 00:21:13,900
However,
finding him won't be easy.

404
00:21:14,033 --> 00:21:15,300
I'm sure
he is already in hiding.

405
00:21:15,433 --> 00:21:16,700
He vanished into thin air.

406
00:21:17,767 --> 00:21:19,167
[BORROMEO] Ma'am Sam.

407
00:21:19,300 --> 00:21:21,800
I just came from Chinatown,
and I saw something.

408
00:21:21,933 --> 00:21:24,867
A clearance sale poster
right at Mr. Chan's store.

409
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Ah, pretty smart.

410
00:21:27,133 --> 00:21:28,967
It's one of the oldest
tricks in the books.

411
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:32,233
He'll go into hiding,
and then after a while,

412
00:21:32,367 --> 00:21:34,900
open the business again
under a different name.

413
00:21:35,467 --> 00:21:38,333
We need to sell all this gold.
Give it all a discount.

414
00:21:38,467 --> 00:21:39,533
Sell everything out!

415
00:21:39,667 --> 00:21:41,333
Sir, why are we
selling it at a loss?

416
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:43,267
I'm going on a vacation.

417
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:45,033
I won't come back
for a long time.

418
00:21:45,167 --> 00:21:48,067
And I need money!
More money!

419
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:50,800
Sell all the gold!

420
00:21:50,933 --> 00:21:52,300
[CASTOR] That only means
one thing.

421
00:21:52,433 --> 00:21:55,700
We need to start moving
before they do.

422
00:21:55,833 --> 00:21:58,667
He's in a hurry
to get rid of all the gold.

423
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:00,567
[MONEY THUDS]

424
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:03,967
We have to act right now.
There is no other choice.

425
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:06,133
We need to set
the next stage in motion.

426
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:09,167
Let's just make sure that
Sir Delgado doesn't catch us.

427
00:22:10,167 --> 00:22:11,900
Absolutely.
It's just us on this.

428
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:14,767
This case is a personal
matter for me.

429
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:17,867
I won't stop until Alias Tiger
is held accountable.

430
00:22:18,700 --> 00:22:20,167
Especially those
who are working with him.

431
00:22:22,133 --> 00:22:24,833
[LAO] Boss, we have
done what you ordered.

432
00:22:26,233 --> 00:22:27,200
Show him, Lee.

433
00:22:27,333 --> 00:22:29,067
[LEE] We've found
some information

434
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:32,367
about the NCIA agent
you're looking for.

435
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:33,467
[GLASS CLINKS]

436
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:36,400
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

437
00:22:36,533 --> 00:22:37,867
What do you know about her?

438
00:22:38,233 --> 00:22:40,333
Her name is Samantha Jacinto.

439
00:22:40,467 --> 00:22:43,067
The youngest daughter
of the former NLEA Chief,

440
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:44,600
General Ricardo Jacinto,

441
00:22:45,133 --> 00:22:47,800
and Beauty Queen,
Isobel Jacinto.

442
00:22:48,600 --> 00:22:50,200
[LAO] She has a sister
who's a police officer,

443
00:22:50,367 --> 00:22:52,167
Maxine Jacinto.

444
00:22:52,300 --> 00:22:54,967
Well, it isn't hard to find her.

445
00:22:55,300 --> 00:23:01,500
You can find everything
about her on the internet.

446
00:23:01,633 --> 00:23:03,267
She arrested Victor.

447
00:23:03,867 --> 00:23:05,800
We need to teach
her a lesson.

448
00:23:07,200 --> 00:23:08,200
Lucas.

449
00:23:08,333 --> 00:23:15,400
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

450
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:17,600
Stop worrying about that.

451
00:23:18,433 --> 00:23:20,300
We have a bigger problem.

452
00:23:21,767 --> 00:23:22,967
What is it?

453
00:23:23,100 --> 00:23:24,333
It's Mr. Chan.

454
00:23:25,067 --> 00:23:28,267
I'm pretty sure they're going
to use Mr. Chan

455
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:31,000
as a witness against Victor.

456
00:23:31,133 --> 00:23:34,267
We need to make sure
that he doesn't talk.

457
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:37,267
We'll take care of him.

458
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:40,500
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC
CONTINUES, FADES]

459
00:23:40,633 --> 00:23:47,533
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

460
00:24:02,500 --> 00:24:04,333
<i> Whoever you are...</i>

461
00:24:05,967 --> 00:24:08,567
<i>you clearly don't know
who you're messing with.</i>

462
00:24:08,700 --> 00:24:10,500
Get me out of here!

463
00:24:13,633 --> 00:24:16,867
<i>Once I get out of here,
I'll collect you myself!</i>

464
00:24:18,467 --> 00:24:20,333
<i>I'll get you
and your whole family!</i>

465
00:24:20,967 --> 00:24:22,700
[SCREAMS]

466
00:24:22,833 --> 00:24:27,433
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

467
00:24:27,567 --> 00:24:32,467
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

468
00:24:32,633 --> 00:24:34,567
[LINE RINGING]

469
00:24:34,700 --> 00:24:38,833
[CELLPHONE RINGING]

470
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:41,200
Hello?

471
00:24:41,333 --> 00:24:43,200
Hello? Ah, Mr. Chan!

472
00:24:43,333 --> 00:24:44,300
Who is this?

473
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:47,000
[CHUCKLES] My name
is Carlota Diaz.

474
00:24:47,133 --> 00:24:49,300
<i>I went to your store
yesterday, remember?</i>

475
00:24:49,433 --> 00:24:50,667
Oh, yes.

476
00:24:50,800 --> 00:24:52,233
Beautiful girl.

477
00:24:52,367 --> 00:24:53,433
Why did you call?

478
00:24:53,567 --> 00:24:56,833
I was hoping to buy some
jewelry from you for my store.

479
00:24:56,967 --> 00:24:59,333
I need quite a lot of them.

480
00:24:59,467 --> 00:25:01,700
You might have some
good designs available.

481
00:25:03,033 --> 00:25:04,867
My budget is 5 million.

482
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:07,067
What made you decide to buy now?

483
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:10,567
[SAM]<i> There's a festival
</i> coming up in my province.

484
00:25:10,700 --> 00:25:13,233
I thought about how
there are a lot of buyers there,

485
00:25:13,367 --> 00:25:15,067
it would such a waste
of my potential earnings.

486
00:25:15,200 --> 00:25:16,567
[MR. CHAN] I understand.

487
00:25:16,700 --> 00:25:19,167
<i>I'll give you
a big discount today.</i>

488
00:25:20,367 --> 00:25:23,233
There's a clearance sale.
I'll give you good-quality gold.

489
00:25:23,367 --> 00:25:25,933
Alright.
Should I stop by your store?

490
00:25:26,067 --> 00:25:27,600
[MR. CHAN] No, no.
Not in the store.

491
00:25:28,100 --> 00:25:29,533
My store is closed today.

492
00:25:29,667 --> 00:25:30,800
I'll meet you at the warehouse.

493
00:25:31,500 --> 00:25:33,700
Okay? I'll text you the address.

494
00:25:33,833 --> 00:25:35,033
All right, sir. See you.

495
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:37,200
Okay. I'll see you there.

496
00:25:37,333 --> 00:25:41,200
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

497
00:25:43,300 --> 00:25:49,400
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

498
00:25:49,533 --> 00:25:51,067
Pops, Gabo is here.

499
00:25:53,300 --> 00:25:54,967
- Tatang.
- Gabo!

500
00:25:55,833 --> 00:25:57,667
I knew you'd come back.

501
00:25:57,800 --> 00:25:59,333
I know you need my help

502
00:25:59,467 --> 00:26:01,900
because your father
is in the hospital

503
00:26:02,033 --> 00:26:03,733
and is fighting for his life.

504
00:26:03,867 --> 00:26:06,867
You know, Gabo,
nothing escapes Pops.

505
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:08,633
He knows everything about you.

506
00:26:08,800 --> 00:26:13,100
Because we keep tabs on you
24 hours a day.

507
00:26:13,233 --> 00:26:16,800
We follow your every move
at all times.

508
00:26:16,933 --> 00:26:19,667
We always have
eyes on you, Gabo.

509
00:26:19,800 --> 00:26:23,333
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

510
00:26:23,467 --> 00:26:26,700
Tatang, I would like
to make it up to you

511
00:26:26,833 --> 00:26:28,667
because I really need your help.

512
00:26:28,800 --> 00:26:30,633
Is there a mission
you can give me?

513
00:26:30,767 --> 00:26:32,533
I have a mission for you.

514
00:26:32,667 --> 00:26:37,367
When Victor Zafra was arrested
by the NCIA,

515
00:26:38,533 --> 00:26:42,467
Mr. Chan was able to
snag the gold bars.

516
00:26:42,633 --> 00:26:44,100
This is our chance to catch
the accomplice

517
00:26:44,233 --> 00:26:45,133
of the gold-smuggling syndicate.

518
00:26:45,267 --> 00:26:46,833
I called Mr. Chan.

519
00:26:46,967 --> 00:26:49,233
He'll meet with me
to sell me gold.

520
00:26:49,367 --> 00:26:52,467
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

521
00:26:52,600 --> 00:26:54,467
Where can I find Mr. Chan?

522
00:26:54,600 --> 00:26:58,833
You'll find him at a warehouse
in Plaza Mayor

523
00:26:58,967 --> 00:27:00,167
on Cristobal Street.

524
00:27:00,300 --> 00:27:01,600
[SAM] That's where he'll bring
the gold.

525
00:27:01,733 --> 00:27:03,667
And that's where
we'll catch him.

526
00:27:03,800 --> 00:27:05,433
After that, we'll bring him
to Sir Delgado.

527
00:27:05,567 --> 00:27:07,533
[LAWIN] That's where he
does his transactions.

528
00:27:07,667 --> 00:27:08,733
He's meeting a buyer tonight.

529
00:27:08,867 --> 00:27:10,700
If you want to find him,
go there.

530
00:27:10,833 --> 00:27:12,900
We'll make our move tonight.

531
00:27:13,767 --> 00:27:15,300
I'll be needing your help.

532
00:27:15,933 --> 00:27:20,033
You must take the gold
from Mr. Chan.

533
00:27:21,467 --> 00:27:24,033
I don't care if he dies or not.

534
00:27:24,167 --> 00:27:25,967
[ROBERT]<i> They have eyes
</i> and ears everywhere,

535
00:27:26,100 --> 00:27:27,167
so we must be careful,

536
00:27:27,300 --> 00:27:28,567
or they might intercept
our plan.

537
00:27:28,700 --> 00:27:32,133
Because his transaction with
Victor Zafra was intercepted,

538
00:27:32,267 --> 00:27:34,333
he doubled their men.

539
00:27:34,467 --> 00:27:38,200
He knows he'll be the police's
next target.

540
00:27:38,333 --> 00:27:43,767
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

541
00:27:43,900 --> 00:27:45,400
[GUNS COCKING]

542
00:27:46,767 --> 00:27:48,867
[CLICKING]

543
00:27:49,433 --> 00:27:51,967
With this, we can finally prove
that you're a great leader, Sam.

544
00:27:52,100 --> 00:27:53,433
It will clear your name,

545
00:27:53,567 --> 00:27:55,433
and your job won't be
at risk anymore.

546
00:27:55,567 --> 00:27:57,500
Thank you very much,
everyone.

547
00:27:57,633 --> 00:27:59,633
[PAPANG] You can do it, Gabo.

548
00:28:00,500 --> 00:28:03,667
You've proven yourself to me
when we were in jail.

549
00:28:04,467 --> 00:28:06,600
I know you won't let us down.

550
00:28:10,700 --> 00:28:17,700
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

551
00:28:28,033 --> 00:28:30,233
<i>This is the target.
A small-time reporter.</i>

552
00:28:30,367 --> 00:28:32,033
<i>- Salvador.
- I won't fight back!</i>

553
00:28:32,167 --> 00:28:33,833
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING]

554
00:28:33,967 --> 00:28:35,767
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVS]

555
00:28:36,833 --> 00:28:38,667
[LOUD THUDS]

556
00:28:40,567 --> 00:28:42,233
This is Mr. Chan's calling card.

557
00:28:42,367 --> 00:28:43,200
<i> I'm here.</i>

558
00:28:43,333 --> 00:28:44,867
<i>I think this is where
they're going.</i>

559
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:47,333
<i>They are acting without
my permission!</i>

560
00:28:47,467 --> 00:28:48,367
<i> You want gold bars?</i>

561
00:28:48,500 --> 00:28:50,133
<i>Go on a date with me.
Let's go to China!</i>

562
00:28:50,267 --> 00:28:51,467
Brace yourselves.

563
00:28:51,600 --> 00:28:53,067
<i>- Who's that?!
- Men, move in! Go!</i>

564
00:28:53,200 --> 00:28:54,433
Because the search...

565
00:28:54,567 --> 00:28:56,600
<i>Mr. Chan! We're being
attacked by the Zafras!</i>

566
00:28:56,767 --> 00:28:59,567
...will end in an
intense encounter.

567
00:28:59,700 --> 00:29:01,333
- [SCREAMING]
- [GUNSHOTS]

568
00:29:01,467 --> 00:29:05,200
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING]

569
00:29:05,333 --> 00:29:06,367
[GUNSHOT]
